  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A rise in cyberattacks, sabotage and information operations against tech firms increases incident response and hardening costs and forces postponement or rollback of model deployments, slowing the cadence of new releases.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_europe_war</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_global_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_europe_war::hybrid_attack_frequency" target="bond_market_shock::funding_market_stress" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A rise in hybrid attacks (cyber, sabotage) increases counterparty and operational risk in payment, settlement and repo systems, prompting lenders to pull back and increasing margin calls and haircuts, thereby elevating funding-market stress.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_europe_war</data>
  <data key="d39">bond_market_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_europe_war::hybrid_attack_frequency" target="us_iran_standoff::export_route_security" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.55</data>
  <data key="d36">An uptick in hybrid attacks (drones, sabotage, cyber on ports and shipping) in the Russia–Europe context spreads techniques, matériel flows, and permissive norms that enable similar attacks on commercial shipping in the Gulf and Strait of Hormuz, directly degrading export-route security.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_europe_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_standoff</data>
