<edge source="us_iran_standoff::export_route_security" target="ai_global_rivalry::chip_supply_constraint" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">Attacks, interdictions or insurance shocks on key shipping lanes (e.g., Strait of Hormuz routes) directly increase transit times, rerouting costs and insurer refusals for high-value semiconductor wafers and fab equipment, producing immediate supply bottlenecks and longer lead times for AI-capable hardware.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_iran_standoff</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_global_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_standoff::export_route_security" target="bond_market_shock::funding_market_stress" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Deterioration in export-route security (e.g., attacks on tankers) raises insurance and counterparty risk and forces banks/treasuries to pull or reprice short-term credit lines for trade finance, increasing stress in wholesale funding markets.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_iran_standoff</data>
  <data key="d39">bond_market_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_standoff::export_route_security" target="china_regional_power::supply_chain_shift_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">Measured declines in security along Gulf and nearby maritime routes (attacks, seizures, insurance spikes) directly raise transport and transit risk for Chinese importers and exporters, prompting firms to accelerate diversification and relocation of suppliers and routings.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_iran_standoff</data>
  <data key="d39">china_regional_power</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_standoff::export_route_security" target="russia_europe_war::energy_price_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">A deterioration in security of Persian Gulf/Red Sea export routes reduces physical flows and raises short‑term risk premia, directly pushing up global and European refined fuel prices as traders anticipate lost cargoes and insurance costs rise.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_iran_standoff</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_europe_war</data>
