  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Sharp increases in the official short-term policy rate create near-term economic pain (market losses, higher borrowing costs and job risks) that incentivize political actors to adopt hawkish rhetoric and pressure for assertive measures abroad to shift public attention and signal resolve.</data>
