<edge source="bond_market_shock::funding_market_stress" target="ai_global_rivalry::model_release_cadence" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Elevated funding stress raises short‑term borrowing costs and triggers margin calls for AI firms and cloud customers, prompting them to delay compute‑intensive R&amp;D and product rollouts and thus slow the cadence of model releases.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">bond_market_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_global_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bond_market_shock::funding_market_stress" target="china_regional_power::interest_rate_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">A rise in wholesale funding stress pushes up interbank and term funding costs, which is passed through to benchmark lending and market rates as banks repricing liquidity raise offered borrowing costs absent offsetting central‑bank easing.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">bond_market_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">china_regional_power</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bond_market_shock::funding_market_stress" target="russia_europe_war::transport_logistics_capa" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Acute funding stress raises short-term borrowing and collateral costs for shipping, freight forwarders and fuel storage operators, forcing route cuts, deferred sailings and reduced working-capital financing that directly shrinks operational transport and distribution capacity.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">bond_market_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_europe_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bond_market_shock::funding_market_stress" target="russia_europe_war::emergency_policy_interve" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">When funding markets seize up and energy traders, utilities or importers face margin calls or imminent cash shortfalls, governments and central banks directly deploy emergency credit lines, guarantees or inventory releases to avert supply stoppages.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">bond_market_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_europe_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bond_market_shock::funding_market_stress" target="us_iran_standoff::military_presence_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Acute wholesale funding stress raises short-term financing costs for defense contractors, logistics providers and overseas base operations, prompting commanders to postpone rotations, defer nonessential deployments and temporarily reduce forward force levels.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">bond_market_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_standoff</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bond_market_shock::cat::fed_october_rate_hike" target="bond_market_shock::policy_rate_expectations" id="0">
