<edge source="china_regional_power::technology_restrictions" target="china_regional_power::supply_chain_shift_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">intra_causal</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
</edge>
<edge source="china_regional_power::technology_restrictions" target="ai_global_rivalry::model_release_cadence" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Tighter formal limits on cross‑border data flows, joint research and tech transfer reduce Chinese labs' access to foreign datasets, collaboration partners and sometimes cloud/compute, slowing development and public releases of new models.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">china_regional_power</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_global_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="china_regional_power::technology_restrictions" target="bond_market_shock::nominal_long_yield" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A sudden tightening of formal technology transfer and data‑flow restrictions raises near‑term geopolitical and growth uncertainty for global tech supply chains, triggering safe‑haven flows into long‑dated sovereign bonds and pushing nominal long yields down.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
